    answer: `SHA-256 (Secure Hash Algorithm 256-bit) represents a cryptographic hash algorithm generating a fixed-length 64-character hexadecimal result (256 bits) from any given input text or information. It was created by the United States National Security Agency (NSA) and released by NIST in 2001 as a component of the SHA-2 collection. SHA-256 operates through a sequence of mathematical functions — bitwise actions (AND, OR, XOR, NOT), modular arithmetic, and message scheduling — executed across 64 compression cycles to transform input data into a deterministic, fixed-size digest. The core traits granting SHA-256 cryptographic value are: (1) Determinism — identical inputs always yield identical hashes. (2) Pre-image resistance — reversing the hash back to the original input remains computationally impractical. (3) Avalanche effect — altering even a single character within the input results in an entirely distinct hash. (4) Collision resistance — discovering two unique inputs yielding the same hash proves computationally impossible given current technology. Our SHA256 generator computes hashes completely inside your browser via the Web Crypto API, guaranteeing your data never departs your device.`,
